Z||000000||Loki has a dream||07-17-2001||10:33 PM||||I have an 85 GT The other day I was letting it run (I dont have it on the road yet)after awile it shut down aparently due to overheating.Well today I started it up,I have to jump start it (batt won't hold a charge)It started right up,but when I took off the jumper cables it puttered and died. I then jumped it again .it started right up and again when I disconected it puttered and stalled.Can any one tell me what might be wrong or at least some place to start looking?Do you think the over heating killed something vitel in the car? Thanks for your time,James||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||07-17-2001||10:41 PM||||Sounds like you have a bad alternator and/or battery.  If the car runs while you have it hooked up to another car and dies when you unhook the jumper cables normally means you have a dead battery or alternator, or both!<P>Good luck<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">         <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||07-17-2001||10:47 PM||||preach it FieroMaster88<P>no doubt about it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||PBJ||07-17-2001||10:48 PM||||Ohhhh and welcome.  ehhhh.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||07-17-2001||10:48 PM||||It could be your alternator and/or your battery. If a battery is really low and the alternator is dead there won't be enough voltage to keep the car running. Have you tried charging the battery? Does something appear to be draining it or will it go dead even if it's disconnected? Do you have a voltmeter? With a good battery and alternator voltage should be around 12.5 with the car off and around 14 with it running.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||07-17-2001||10:50 PM||||I type too slow... looks like mines the third vote for Altenator and/or battery. ||||reg||10
