Z||000007||Raydar||07-17-2001||10:55 PM||||Welcome to the Forum! <BR>Interesting username, BTW. We already have a Loki.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>If you rev it up to around 2500, and then remove the jumper cables, does it still die?<BR>If so, I would bet on the alternator. <BR>The battery *may* be okay, once it gets a good charge. <BR>Then again, if the battery has an internal short, it may have killed the alternator. <P>Are you sure about the overheating?<BR>That usually causes all sorts of *other* nasty symptoms. Usually accompanied by leaks, unpleasant noises, and/or interchange of vital fluids (water in oil, etc.)<BR>Does it sound okay? No smoke or clattering? <BR> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||RacinRob||07-17-2001||10:56 PM||||Heat and electronics don't mix well.... it may have been going out and the over heating cooked it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||StuGood||07-18-2001||09:46 AM||||Did your belts disappear (not the ones in your dresser drawer - the ones in your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> )?  Or, could they have started slipping for some reason?  That would explain the overheating (no water pump) and no charge.<P>Also, no charge for all this free advice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ||||reg||5
